 of early European musical film. Their songs for productions associated with singers such as Richard Tauber and Jan Kiepura were not simply film numbers: they were designed to travel beyond the screen as printed music, recordings, radio items, and repertory for performers. This star-singer circuit explains why the duo’s European experience later appeared useful to MGM, which read it through the promotional language of Viennese musical competence.","roles":["industry_context","career_mechanism","professional_network"],"personIds":["P009","P077","P117","P118"],"sourceIds":["SRC0490","SRC0491","SRC0551"],"workIds":["W-F007","W-F011","W-F023","W-S076"],"mediaIds":["M031","M155","M167","M192","M229"],"heroMediaIds":["M229"],"placeIds":["PL002","PL003","PL030"],"periods":["european"]},{"id":"TE0052","slug":"ninon-mayer-ritz-meeting-mgm-contract","title":"Ninon reaches Louis B. Mayer: the Ritz meeting and MGM contract","label":"Ninon opens the MGM path","displayDate":"August 1934","dateStart":"1934-08-07","datePrecision":"circa_year","sortDate":"1934-08-07","sortOrder":33.5,"displayMode":"point","eventType":"career","period":"european","periodKey":"european","category":"migration","filterTags":["career","europe"],"placeDisplay":"Paris","cityKey":"paris","shortDescription":"The European success of Ninon reportedly brought Kaper and Jurmann to the attention of Louis B. Mayer, leading to a meeting at the Hôtel Ritz and an MGM contract.","longDescription":"Kaper later recalled that the success of Ninon—written for Tout pour l’amour, the French version of Ein Lied für Dich—was the turning point that opened the path to Hollywood. During his European talent-scouting trip in August 1934, Louis B. Mayer reportedly asked to meet the song’s authors, heard them perform at the Hôtel Ritz, and offered a seven-year MGM contract.","featured":true,"roles":["career_milestone","migration_event","professional_network"],"personIds":["P009","P077","P116","P117"],"sourceIds":["SRC0491","SRC0494"],"workIds":["W-F023","W-F025","W-S076","W-S077"],"mediaIds":["M034","M051"],"heroMediaIds":["M051"],"placeIds":["PL003","PL023","PL038"],"periods":["european"]}],"places":[],"contributions":[{"id":"CON-S076-C-P009","role":"composer","nameAsPrinted":"B. Kaper","sortOrder":10,"certainty":"confirmed","workIds":["W-S076"],"personIds":["P009"],"sourceIds":["SRC0190"],"nameVariantIds":["PNV0019"]},{"id":"CON-S076-C-P077","role":"composer","nameAsPrinted":"Walter Jurmann","sortOrder":11,"certainty":"confirmed","workIds":["W-S076"],"personIds":["P077"],"sourceIds":["SRC0190"]},{"id":"CON-S076-L-P020","role":"lyricist","nameAsPrinted":"Fritz Rotter","sortOrder":1,"certainty":"confirmed","workIds":["W-S076"],"personIds":["P020"],"sourceIds":["SRC0190"]},{"id":"CON-S076-LAB-ORG128","role":"record_label","nameAsPrinted":"Odeon","displayCredit":"Issuing label","evidenceContext":"online_catalogue","sortOrder":60,"certainty":"confirmed","workIds":["W-S076"],"organizationIds":["ORG150"],"sourceIds":["SRC0730"],"scopeNote":"Issued the recording on its red label in 1933, according to the upload; no catalogue number is given."},{"id":"CON-S076-P-ORG120","role":"performer","nameAsPrinted":"Odeon-Künstler-Orchester","displayCredit":"Orchestra","evidenceContext":"online_catalogue","sortOrder":56,"certainty":"confirmed","workIds":["W-S076"],"organizationIds":["ORG120"],"sourceIds":["SRC0730"],"scopeNote":"Accompanied Jan Kiepura on the Odeon pressing of 1933, under Dr. Weissmann; the label is not shown."},{"id":"CON-S076-P-P117","role":"performer","nameAsPrinted":"Jan Kiepura","displayCredit":"Vocal performance","evidenceContext":"recording_label","sortOrder":50,"certainty":"confirmed","workIds":["W-S076"],"personIds":["P117"],"sourceIds":["SRC0583"]},{"id":"CON-S076-PUB-ORG029","role":"publisher","nameAsPrinted":"Wiener Boheme Verlag","evidenceContext":"sheet_music","certainty":"confirmed","workIds":["W-S076"],"organizationIds":["ORG029"],"sourceIds":["SRC0190"]}],"personNameVariants":[